Package: cqtna
Title: Context-Specific QTL Target Nomination Audit
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R:
    person("MR audit project", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "noreply@example.com")
Description: Runs the automatable part of eight diagnostics on a candidate list
    produced by any cis-eQTL-instrumented Mendelian randomization pipeline, and
    reports what kind of evidence each gene actually carries. Checks locus
    attribution against the outcome's own known loci by independent locus, with a
    mismatched-list negative control; recomputes the significant list over four
    inference units; measures list stability against a second outcome GWAS;
    reports instrument availability at three separate levels; computes
    compartment attribution and eQTL-to-GWAS peak distance; and sweeps the two
    window conventions that a fold enrichment depends on. Three of the eight
    diagnostics cannot be automated from a candidate list and are named in every
    report rather than omitted.
